reviews.text:
The rooms are the highlight, but besides that:
- beach is dirty;
- besides staff being gentle, the service is super slow and everyone keep pushing Melia Membership on every chance they have;
- bartenders save a lot in the alcohol from the drinks + only 1 type of beer (local);
- food is eatable (6 out of 10), but desert is terrible;
- don’t expect to go to all the restaurants, only a few are available for regular guests and only for dinner;
- a lot of exclusive areas for Circle Members or guests from The Reserve lower the regular guests experience bar, that are restricted to 1 bar at the main pool and 1 restaurant (The Lunch Box);
- no bar close to the beach and you will only see a waiter once in the full-moon.
- staff can be very noisy around the rooms, even early in the morning.
